description:
FOUND by s538b (#2371).  perl 5.40.3:
  package A1; our $AUTOLOAD; sub new { bless {}, shift } sub AUTOLOAD { print "AUTOLOAD $AUTOLOAD\n"; return }
  package main; my $o = A1->new; $o->DESTROY; print "after\n";
  perl: AUTOLOAD A1::DESTROY / after (and again at global destruction)
  PCL:  dies `Can't locate object method "DESTROY" via package "A1"` (pre-existing: the base prints the same).
Cause: %pcl-dispatch-autoload and %pcl-super-autoload in cl/pcl-runtime.lisp both start `(unless (string-equal method-name "DESTROY") ...)` -- an exclusion with no recorded reason (an old guard against an implicit-DESTROY path that never existed?).  perl excludes nothing for an explicit call.  The exit-time destruction s538b built does its own resolution (%p-destroy-method) and calls AUTOLOAD as perl does.  Fix = delete the two exclusions, guard row, probe a SUPER:: spelling.
